WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:17.082
Hi! Comprehension questions come in a few kinds: finding information, inferring, working out what it or they refers to, true or false, and putting events in order. Today we'll practise each one with a short passage.

2
00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:23.922
For literal questions, the answer is written in the text. Circle the key words and look back.

3
00:00:24.072 --> 00:00:32.874
For inference questions, the answer is not written. Use clues from what the characters do and say. Biting your lip shows worry.

4
00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:40.578
Referencing questions ask what it, they or this refers to. Look back for the nearest noun and put it in to check.

5
00:00:40.728 --> 00:00:49.170
For true or false, give a reason from the text. For sequencing, follow the order of events in the story.

6
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:55.938
Watch out! If the question asks how Ravi felt, writing just he bit his lip is not enough!

7
00:00:56.088 --> 00:01:00.450
Name the feeling first, then use because to give the evidence.

8
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.706
Like this: he felt worried because he bit his lip.

9
00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:15.714
Your turn! Read the passage first. Where did Ravi find the puppy? Pause and think.

10
00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:23.154
Behind the bins near the market. That is a literal question. Did you get it right?

11
00:01:23.304 --> 00:01:31.386
Here's another! What did Ravi give the puppy? Pause and think.

12
00:01:31.536 --> 00:01:36.714
Some water from his bottle. Did you get it right?

13
00:01:36.864 --> 00:01:46.266
Another one! How did Ravi feel when he found the puppy, and why? Pause and think.

14
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:54.354
He felt worried, because he bit his lip. That is an inference question. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:54.504 --> 00:02:03.954
Next one! It was wet and shivering. What does it refer to? Pause and think.

16
00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:11.658
The puppy. Look back for the nearest noun: a tiny puppy. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:11.808 --> 00:02:22.362
Here's another! Ravi kept the puppy. True or false? Give a reason. Pause and think.

18
00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:31.386
False. They took the puppy to the animal shelter, and later a kind family adopted it. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:31.536 --> 00:02:42.138
Last one! Put these in order: gave it water, heard a cry, took it to the shelter. Pause and think.

20
00:02:42.288 --> 00:02:50.226
First he heard a cry, then he gave it water, and last they took it to the shelter. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:50.376 --> 00:03:00.594
Remember: for literal questions, look back. For inference, name the feeling and give a reason. For referencing, find the noun and put it back in.

22
00:03:00.744 --> 00:03:06.738
For true or false, give a reason. For sequencing, follow the order of the story.

23
00:03:06.888 --> 00:03:13.290
After reading a story today, tell someone how the main character felt and why!

